    public DocumentDefinition Create() => DocumentDefinition.Create(ScribeNode.Create(
        "LatticeCosetChargedJacobi", H("All-state charged Jacobi for the actual compressed fields"), Blocks(
            Paragraph(Text("Let D be the original finite-rank integral even lattice data, e an arbitrary finite external rank, B an arbitrary integral cross block, and C an arbitrary symmetric integral block with even diagonal. Both ranks include zero. The theorem assumes positive definiteness only of the ORIGINAL gramReal D. There is no positive-definiteness, nondegeneracy or inverse hypothesis on the ambient block. I denotes the existing compressed D B C hC hCe, with the original injection, projection, all-state field and lattice cocycle unchanged. S denotes the full schur D B C: its C contribution and inverse-original-Gram cross-block correction are both retained. All source and input states range over the entire original Carrier D, including arbitrary finite charge sums and oscillator polynomials.")),
            D("charged_borcherds", "For every such D,e,B,C,hC,hCe, every positive-definiteness proof hD for the original Gram form, every external charge a,b,c, every original u,v,w and every signed integer p,r,s, the actual iterate sum with weight choose(p+S(a,c),i) equals the first ordered product sum with weight (-1)^i choose(r+S(a,b),i), minus (-1)^r times the reverse ordered product sum with that same weight. The iterate modes are (r+i,p+s-i), the first product modes (p+r-i,s+i), and the reverse product modes (r+s-i,p+i). Each summation index i is natural; the modes and shifts remain integral with their displayed signs. These are actual compressed-field compositions in the three composable charge sectors. The statement is the algebraic coefficient identity on every original state, with the literal residue sign and original lattice cocycle conventions.", DescribeRole.Theorem),
            Paragraph(Text("The consumed proof chain first proves projection_oscillator_derivation and projection_translation on the full ambient carrier. Only the original inverse Gram is used to identify the projected translation with moduleL(-1). The symmetry helper schur_swap and the actual reverse_contraction enter source_mixed. Source skew symmetry, translation transport and the existing product contraction give choose(S(a,c),n) with NO extra (-1)^n. The consumed exact_source_probe then reconstructs the projected ambient iterate from the actual inner creation expansion; it does not posit an independently coherent family.")),
            Paragraph(Text("The private binomial_convolution proves the necessary finite triangular interchange for an arbitrary complex module: the two nested sums weighted by z^i choose(x,i) and z^j choose(y,j) collapse to the sum weighted by z^k choose(x+y,k) on f(k). Its hypothesis is an actual vector tail cutoff. The joint support lies in i+j<N before finsum_curry or diagonal reindexing; the generalized binomial coefficients themselves need not truncate. Ring.add_choose_eq supplies Vandermonde. iterate_cutoff and product_cutoff obtain the required tails from compressed_high_modes before scalar multiplication. integer_choose identifies the existing integral-binomial convention. These helpers are consumed by charged_borcherds; the convolution is also reused by the weak-associativity module.")),
            Paragraph(Text("Finally charged_borcherds applies the existing ordinary all-state ambient Borcherds identity to J(a,u), J(b,v), J(c,w), projects it by P(a+b+c), and identifies all three projected summand families. The source correction uses the convolution with z=1 and the two product corrections use z=-1. This finite convolution and projected all-state descent are the mathematical content; bookkeeping applications and cutoff helpers supply no separate novelty claim or artificial new endpoint.")),
            Paragraph(Text("At a=0 the displayed Schur terms vanish. For C=0 the existing neutral supplier identifies the neutral compressed action with the ORIGINAL action in the appropriate B-labelled module. For the canonical rational reindexing at C=0, q_ab=-S(a,b) and K_ab(u)[m-q_ab]v=I_ab(u)[m]v, with raw rational q rather than q modulo integers. These are parameter correspondences in the exposition, not additional named application theorems.")),
            Paragraph(Text("Source attribution: the supplied LatticeCosetChargedJacobi mathematical source, including its source-contraction attribution to LatticeCosetSourceSkewProbe.lean, SHA256 73fa8b8332d3fa5e57ebe74d853682c869cf39031724cdc088191c004e5a84ce. The imported LatticeCosetOperatorCorrection, LatticeDualCosetVirasoro, StateField.SkewSymmetry and LatticeAllStateJacobi remain the native suppliers. Classical lattice conventions are Bakalov--Kac, math/0402315v1, section 4.1; native residue and Sugawara sources retain their Scott Carnahan and Kalle Kytölä attributions. This document makes no claim of literature novelty, analytic sewing, an actual quotient F or exchange theorem, scalar polynomiality, categorical or physical realization, or string/AdS completion.")))));
}
